    zh: { keywords: ['心碎', '悲伤', '分离', '真相', '失望', '疗愈'], dailyU: '今天可能面对令人难过的事实。允许情绪经过，不必假装坚强，诚实是疗愈的起点。', dailyR: '今天适合释放旧伤，但要避免反复刺痛自己。原谅不等于否认，而是停止让伤口控制现在。', upright: '宝剑三正位代表心碎、失望、分离与不可回避的痛苦真相。看见伤口虽然艰难，却让真正的疗愈成为可能。', reversed: '宝剑三逆位代表恢复、释放悲伤，或旧伤仍被压抑并反复影响关系。你需要给痛苦一个被理解的位置。', intro: '三把剑刺入心脏，是塔罗中最直接的悲伤图像。它说明思想、话语或事实也能造成真实的情感伤害。', lesson: '它的核心不是永远停在心碎，而是让真相穿过之后，慢慢把心还给自己。' },
    en: { keywords: ['heartbreak', 'grief', 'separation', 'truth', 'disappointment', 'healing'], dailyU: 'A painful truth may surface. Let emotion move through you; honesty begins healing.', dailyR: 'Release an old wound without reopening it repeatedly. Forgiveness means the wound no longer rules the present.', upright: 'The Three of Swords upright represents heartbreak, disappointment, separation, and painful truth. Seeing the wound makes genuine healing possible.', reversed: 'Reversed, it represents recovery and release, or an old wound still suppressed and shaping relationships.', intro: 'Three blades pierce a heart, showing how thoughts, words, and facts can cause real emotional injury.', lesson: 'The card does not ask you to live in heartbreak, but to reclaim your heart after truth passes through.' },
